skill: "vendor-sla-breach-watch"
sections[3]:
  - "# vendor-sla-breach-watch\n\nMaintain the SLA register per vendor contract, collect breach evidence, compute credits owed and escalate repeat offenders. Use when an incident touches a vendor-managed service, when a monthly vendor report lands, or when a credit claim deadline is close. Feeds SRE error-budget reviews with vendor-side context.\n\nOwner: role-procurement-vendor-manager (pod-gna, procurement). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"SLA definitions per contract (availability, response, resolution, credits); incident records from SRE; vendor monthly reports; credit claim deadlines per contract\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/procurement/sla-register.toon; breach-log.toon with evidence[] and credit_claims[]; escalation list for repeat breaches\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load the SLA definitions per active contract; a vendor without measurable SLAs is recorded as such so the gap is visible instead of implied.\n2. For each incident or vendor report touching a registered service, extract the measured values and compare against the contractual target; compute the miss in the contract's own units.\n3. Classify severity per the contract's matrix; if the contract has no severity matrix, record the breach but mark credits as not-claimable so nobody invents entitlements.\n4. Collect evidence per breach: timeline, error budgets, vendor ticket references and the exact SLA clause number; a claim without clause evidence is not filed.\n5. Compute credits owed per the contract formula with run_command; round per contract terms.\n6. Draft the credit claim before its contractual deadline; the deadline is tracked in sla-register.toon and a missed deadline is itself recorded as a process breach.\n7. Track breaches per vendor over rolling 90 days; two or more breaches of the same clause triggers an escalation memo to the operator with a remediation ask.\n8. Write breach-log.toon and hand the SRE-facing extract to role-sre for error-budget context; vendor-side remediation asks go through the operator.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ncredit claims via operator; SRE context to role-sre; repeat breaches to vendor review.\n"
